SUMMARY:Private Screening of American Graffiti at TrueWest with 60’s Diner Dinner at Costeaux & Car Show
DESCRIPTION:Come dressed in your best greaser style and step back in time for this throwback evening. Enjoy a 1960s‑inspired dinner at Costeaux French Bakery—which has served as Healdsburg’s Bakery for over 100 years. The dinner will take place from 5:30-6:45pm\, and will include classic burgers and fries\, root beer floats\, and wine and beer. There will also be vintage cars on display outside\, so you can truly travel back in time. \nAfter dinner\, head to Healdsburg’s film hub\, True West Film Center\, for a private 7:15pm screening of George Lucas and Francis Ford Coppola’s coming-of-age classic\, American Graffiti. Filmed in Petaluma\, this 1973 film perfectly encapsulates the sights\, sounds\, and spirit of 1960s America. Concessions will also be available for all attendees. \nOur sincere gratitude to True West Film Center for making this experience possible. \n100% of proceeds from this event go to Boys & Girls Clubs of Sonoma-Marin. These funds support us in providing after-school programs\, summer camps\, and essential resources for 11\,000 local youth—at Clubs from Geyserville to Petaluma. \nTicket sales for this event are live and close on Sunday\, April 26th at 6pm.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/private-screening-of-american-graffiti-at-truewest-with-60s-diner-dinner-at-costeaux-car-show/
LOCATION:Costeaux French Bakery\, 417 Healdsburg Avenue\, Healdsburg\, CA
CATEGORIES:Film,Other
GEO:38.61296;-122.87174
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Costeaux French Bakery 417 Healdsburg Avenue Healdsburg CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=417 Healdsburg Avenue:geo:-122.87174,38.61296
END:VEVENT
